meta {
  name: Filter Bookings by Date
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/booking?checkin=2023-12-31&checkout=2025-01-02
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  checkin: 2023-12-31
  checkout: 2025-01-02
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("returns an array of booking ids", function() {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  Exercises the date-filtering feature of GET /booking. The documented
  contract is "bookings that check in after and check out before the given
  dates".

  The assertions here are deliberately bounded to the stable part of the
  contract (200 + array shape): Restful-Booker's date-filter comparison
  logic is known to be buggy (boundary handling differs from the docs), so
  pinning specific result membership would make the suite flaky against a
  bug this repo doesn't control. In a real engagement the boundary bug
  would be filed and the stronger assertion added once fixed.
}
